{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.TrapezoidRule","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TrapezoidRule","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.IntervalIntegral.IntegrationByParts","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Calculus.Deriv.Pow","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Trigonometric.Deriv","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Log.Deriv"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.abs_trapezoid_sub_integral_log_two_sin_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.abs_trapezoid_sub_integral_log_two_sin_le","kind":"theorem","line":200,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TrapezoidRule.lean#L200-L231","doc":"**The trapezoid bound for `log(2 sin)`.**\n\n`|trapezoid − ∫| ≤ (b−a)³·M/12` on any `[a,b] ⊆ (0,π)` with `1/sin² ≤ M`.\n\nThis is exactly the quantity `QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.kashaevErr_add_reflect`\nproves `ε_k + ε_{N−1−k}` equals, on the cell `[θ, θ+h]`.  Bounding it completes\nthe symmetric half of `qou-mlgp` (A): it is `O(h³)` on the cell, hence `O(h²)`\nagainst the `1/h` of the expansion — one order better than the `O(1/N)` claimed,\nwhich is what leaves all the remaining difficulty in the antisymmetric half. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.hasDerivAt_cos_div_sin","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.hasDerivAt_cos_div_sin","kind":"theorem","line":190,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TrapezoidRule.lean#L190-L198","doc":"`(cos/sin)′ = −1/sin²` on `(0, π)` — the second derivative of `log(2 sin)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.hasDerivAt_log_two_sin","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.hasDerivAt_log_two_sin","kind":"theorem","line":178,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TrapezoidRule.lean#L178-L188","doc":"`(log(2 sin))′ = cos/sin` on `(0, π)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.abs_trapezoid_sub_integral_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.abs_trapezoid_sub_integral_le","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TrapezoidRule.lean#L132-L170","doc":"**The trapezoid error bound.**  `|trapezoid − ∫| ≤ (b−a)³·M/12` when\n`|f″| ≤ M` on `[a,b]`.\n\nThe classical `O(h³)` per-cell estimate — `O(h²)` after summing `1/h` cells —\nand the reason a trapezoid rule sees one order more than a rectangle rule. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.integral_eq_trapezoid_sub","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.integral_eq_trapezoid_sub","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TrapezoidRule.lean#L83-L130","doc":"**The trapezoid rule with its exact error term.**\n\n    ∫_a^b f = ((b−a)/2)·(f a + f b) − ½·∫_a^b (x−a)(b−x)·f″(x) dx\n\nfor any `f` with a second derivative on `[[a,b]]` and `f″` continuous there.\nExact — an identity, not an estimate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.integral_weight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.integral_weight","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TrapezoidRule.lean#L63-L81","doc":"`∫_a^b (x−a)(b−x) dx = (b−a)³/6` — the Peano kernel of the trapezoid rule\nhas total mass `(b−a)³/6`.  This is what turns `sup|f″|` into the `1/12`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}